{"schemaVersion":1,"skill":{"id":"mukul975--anthropic-cybersecurity-skills--auditing-kubernetes-rbac-privilege-escalation","name":"auditing-kubernetes-rbac-privilege-escalation","description":"Finds over-permissive RBAC roles and service-account token abuse paths in a Kubernetes cluster using kubectl auth can-i, rbac-police, kubectl-who-can, and rakkess, tracing which subjects can escalate toward cluster-admin. Use when reviewing who can escalate privileges in a cluster, hunting exploitable RoleBindings during an authorized review, or validating least privilege after an RBAC change. Keywords: RBAC, ClusterRoleBinding, service account token, auth can-i, rbac-police, escalate, bind, impersonate. Do not use for designing and applying hardened RBAC - use implementing-rbac-hardening-for-kubernetes.","category":"Cloud & DevOps","tags":["auditing","kubernetes","rbac","privilege","escalation","finds","over","permissive","roles","service","account","token","abuse","paths","cluster","kubectl","auth","police"],"repo":"mukul975/Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skills","owner":"mukul975","stars":34277,"official":false,"featured":false,"license":"Apache-2.0","licensePath":"skills/auditing-kubernetes-rbac-privilege-escalation/LICENSE","revision":"54a798831d2266a3ca61ce68a7acb80b81160d57","path":"skills/auditing-kubernetes-rbac-privilege-escalation","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mukul975/Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skills/tree/54a798831d2266a3ca61ce68a7acb80b81160d57/skills/auditing-kubernetes-rbac-privilege-escalation","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T11:14:06.196Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-31T04:32:42Z","fileCount":5,"bytes":33877,"sha256":"a378f61cbf38eff15580308606299b2e98beead60f5c0c98cf8821ae5b6ad1a6","historical":false},"files":[{"path":"LICENSE","sourcePath":"skills/auditing-kubernetes-rbac-privilege-escalation/LICENSE","bytes":11255,"sha256":"a941b58ef0ba43a31e24ae7ece1b743a585efed9e37792b9ca063e0798be1cbe","mode":420,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mukul975/Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skill